    [BugFix][SpecDecode] Restore independent RNG for residual resampling (#18657)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Restore the resample-only SALT removed by #17661.
    
    Rejection verification and residual categorical sampling currently use
    the same seed and position. Conditioning that random value on rejection
    biases the recovered token distribution. For a one-hot draft on token 0
    and target probabilities `[0.5, 0.25, 0.25]`, rejected requests always
    recover token 2 instead of sampling tokens 1 and 2 equally.
    
    Restore `RESAMPLE_NOISE_SALT=1 << 29` for random non-bonus residual
    draws. Acceptance, greedy paths and bonus RNG positions keep their
    existing behavior. This PR includes only the SALT restoration and
    regression coverage; runner selection is unchanged.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Random speculative decoding uses an independent RNG domain for
    recovered tokens. Fixed-seed results may change when a draft token is
    rejected. No public API changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - File-scoped manual-stage pre-commit hooks passed for both changed
    Python files.
    - Diff whitespace check passed with CRLF handling for the existing CRLF
    kernel file.
    - Added four end-to-end regression cases in
    `tests/e2e/nightly/single_node/ops/singlecard_ops/triton/test_resample.py`:
    one-hot/full draft logits and rejection at step 0/1.
    - The user reports prior validation of the SALT fix.
    - Ascend A3 NPU validation used the v0.30.0 runtime (vLLM
    `ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607`, PyTorch 2.10.0+cpu,
    torch_npu 2.10.0.post4, Triton-Ascend 3.2.0). The operator and test
    files are identical in both PRs.
    - Baseline without SALT: all four new cases failed with the expected
    recovered-token distribution bias (maximum probability error 0.25 versus
    tolerance 0.03).
    - Final candidate: **31 passed**, including all four new regression
    cases and the 27 existing resample cases.
    - Ran the exact test file from an isolated copy to avoid unrelated
    serving conftest setup: `python3 -m pytest
    --confcutdir=/workspace/validation
    /workspace/validation/test_resample.py -q`. Source/test SHA256 hashes
    were verified against the final PR files.
    - Full serving and performance validation were not run. The NPU run used
    the v0.30.0 dependency set; full main-runtime integration remains a
    CI/reviewer check.
    
    Backport to `releases/v0.30.0`: #18658.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
